<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal bond auction seen just above market level.</title>
<headline>Portugal bond auction seen just above market level.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bids at the Portuguese Treasury's auction of 20 billion escudos of five-year bonds are expected to be slightly above market levels because bonds closed weaker on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Bids should be between 7.60 and 7.70 percent since the banks will be wanting a small premium because of the market's easier tone yesterday,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>The results are expected at around 1000 GMT.</p>
<p>On July 25 the Treasury placed 25.35 billion escudos at an average weighted rate of 8.0161 percent.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon editorial +(351-1) 3538254</p>
